# examtopics-scrapper — local configuration.
# Copy this file to ".env" (which is gitignored) and fill in the values.

# ── examcademy.com session cookie ──────────────────────────────────
# examcademy shows only questions 1-25 to anonymous visitors. To reach the
# rest you must be signed in. The site logs in through Auth0 (email, Google
# or Microsoft), but that flow can't be automated — it has bot protection —
# and Chrome 151 encrypts its cookie store (app-bound encryption), so the
# cookie can't be read from the browser automatically either.
#
# So lend the tool your browser session, once:
#
#   1. Sign in at https://examcademy.com in your browser (Google is fine).
#   2. Open DevTools (F12) -> Network tab.
#   3. Click any document request to examcademy.com (e.g. an /exams/... page).
#   4. Under Request Headers, copy the ENTIRE value of the "Cookie:" header.
#      Make sure it's the request to examcademy.com, NOT auth.examcademy.com.
#   5. Paste it below, on one line, wrapped in quotes.
#
# Verify it worked:  python examcademy.py "<exam url>" --check-auth
# The cookie lasts as long as your browser session; re-copy it when it expires.

EXAMCADEMY_COOKIE=""
